    "created_at": "2018-03-07T07:02:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-07T07:02:41Z",
    "body": "Right. Gecko has no type annotations here, but they have `[SetterThrows]` attribute and it passes [WPT tests](https://wpt.fyi/offscreen-canvas/the-offscreen-canvas/offscreencanvas.constructor.html). So I guess they handle the annotation internally.\r\nFor Chromium, this is what I'm woking on, I want to update the IDL file according to this spec. And using `unsigned long long` or `unsigned long` should be a different issue. (We should discuss if it is practical to set >2^16 for `width` or `height` attributes.)\r\n\r\nI want this PR to make it clear that those attributes are consistent with constructors and WPT.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
